# Line-ending policy. Added 2026-08-13.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS
# ---------------
# core.autocrlf was `false` here with no attributes file, so git stored whatever
# bytes happened to be on disk. The repo drifted to 37 files with LF and 20 with
# CRLF, and any editor or tool that normalised a file silently rewrote every line
# of it — burying the real change inside a whole-file diff.
#
# That happened to confluence_status.py in d8bcbd1: 7 lines actually changed,
# 434 lines shown. `git blame` on that file now points at that commit for every
# line instead of at whoever wrote them.
#
# In this repo an unreadable diff is a safety problem, not a style problem. The
# 1.5-yr WATCH sat unshipped for four weeks, the surveyed ladders for eight days,
# and CC-UP-503's calibration for a day — every one of them a divergence that was
# sitting in plain sight and that nobody could see. Whole-file churn is one more
# way for the next one to hide.
#
# LF because CI runs on ubuntu-latest and live.html is served as a web asset.
# Windows checkouts get LF too; VS Code, PyCharm and modern Notepad handle it.

* text=auto

*.py       text eol=lf
*.html     text eol=lf
*.yml      text eol=lf
*.yaml     text eol=lf
*.csv      text eol=lf
*.json     text eol=lf
*.geojson  text eol=lf
*.md       text eol=lf
*.sql      text eol=lf
*.txt      text eol=lf
*.css      text eol=lf

# Binary — git must never rewrite a byte of these.
*.png      binary
*.jpg      binary
*.pdf      binary
*.db       binary
*.tif      binary
*.zip      binary
# pipeline/state/pair_cache.npz — the InSAR pair cache
*.npz      binary
